WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.730
KIM MANIS: Welcome to this
session on securing, scaling,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.300
and sustaining your data
estate in Microsoft Fabric.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.090
I'm Kim Manis, Corporate
Vice President of Product

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.740
of the Microsoft
Fabric Platform.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.670
We all know AI is
changing the world.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.400
It's enabling everyone to
move faster than ever,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.490
whether it's data professionals
who are implementing code faster

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.680
than ever, analysts
and data citizens

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.540
who are spending less
time finding the data

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.180
and more time getting
into the deep analysis,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.670
and line-of-business
users who can go and ask

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.860
and answer their own
questions without the need

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.860
of an analyst for help.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.950
And this is all great, but
that broad data access

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.250
and generative AI, it does
bring additional risk,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.540
increased risky behavior,
increased risk of data breaches.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.960
And often security professionals
are feeling like that security

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.200
and data culture, they
seem in conflict.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.120
And achieving those goals, they
can feel diametrically opposed,

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.570
whether it's fostering a data
culture by driving broad access

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.230
to data and securing your data
and making sure it's governed

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.720
and people are doing the
right things with the data.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.390
And this is really where
Microsoft Fabric comes in.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.960
Microsoft Fabric allows you to
foster a data-driven culture

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.260
through automated, repeatable,
and governed data development

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.110
in Fabric, and you
can get broad access

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.420
through a single
discoverable data catalog

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.600
with the OneLake catalog that's
accessible everywhere your

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.970
business users and
your developers work,

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.870
whether it's Teams,
Excel, Foundry, and more.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.540
And this is great because it's
easy to discover the data,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.830
find what you're looking for,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.780
ask and answer your
own questions.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.390
But with that comes security

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.970
and making sure your data
is governed and secure,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.370
whether it's through
isolating your sensitive data

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.380
with always-on network security

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.530
and managing data access
centrally at the item, folder,

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.950
row, column level, and being
able to govern your data

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.540
and capacity centrally.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.390
So this allows you to give
broad access to everyone

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.340
in your organization
who needs data,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.310
while making sure they only see
what they're supposed to see,

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.980
and they're only accessing the
data the way they're supposed

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.550
to access it.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.550
And Microsoft Fabric is a
complete end-and data platform,

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.560
covering the whole
gamut of tools,

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.050
all the way from databases,
data integration,

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.810
to our newest capabilities
with Fabric IQ.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.000
And today we're really
going to focus on the admin

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.070
and governance space and
how we're enabling all

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.800
of these workloads,
workloads with key admin

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.840
and governance capabilities.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.620
And Fabric has all the tools
to support every user engaged

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.600
